@scene(300, 30)

// A pair of meshing bevel gears, all lengths in millimetres. A bevel pair
// carries motion around a corner. Each gear is a shaft: its teeth, a hub after
// a chamfer, and a bore drilled through. Both pitch cones share one apex at
// the origin, so shaftAngle is the angle between the shafts and the two pitch
// angles always add up to it. Drag it and the pair stays in mesh -- and the
// gears change size, because a bevel gear's cone distance is fixed by its
// teeth, module and pitch angle rather than being free the way a spur gear's
// thickness is. That is why faceWidth here is a fraction of the cone distance
// instead of a length. Time turns the pair one tooth per second.

// One tooth of travel per second; gear 1 forward, gear 2 back by the ratio.
animate = mod(time, 1);

// Tooth counts, and the module (mm): the tooth size at the outer end.
@range(14, 30) numTeeth1 = 16;
@range(14, 30) numTeeth2 = 24;
@range(2, 10) moduleVal = 5.0;

// Pressure angle of the tooth flanks, in radians (0.35 is about 20 degrees).
@range(0.2, 0.5) pressureAngle = 0.35;

// A right angle by default, but nothing here needs one. The range stops short
// of the shaft angle that would drive the slower gear's pitch cone out toward
// a flat crown, where the back-cone approximation these teeth are built on
// gives out.
@range(0.9, 1.75) shaftAngle = 1.5707963;

// The angle the tooth trace makes with the cone element: 0 is a straight
// bevel, anything else a spiral bevel. Gear 2 takes the opposite hand -- a
// same-hand pair collides instead of meshing.
@range(-1, 1) spiralAngle = 0.5;

// Face width as a fraction of the cone distance; gear practice keeps it
// under about a third.
@range(0.1, 0.4) faceFraction = 0.3;

// The teeth run out on the two cones normal to the pitch cone, and each of
// those is cut by a flat face set this many millimetres along the axis from
// that end's outer tooth-tip corner. Take crownToBack to zero and the back
// face flattens out level with the tips; open it and the face stands proud
// with the tooth heels stepping down to it. recess does the mirror at the
// small end, setting the face back so the teeth project toward the mate.
@range(0, 15) crownToBack = 4.0;
@range(0, 15) recess = 4.0;

// The hub, which on a bevel gear rides the heel: standoffHeight is what it
// projects past the back face. Hub diameters, chamfer and bores are in mm.
@range(0, 25) standoffHeight = 12.0;
standoffDiam1 = 30;
standoffDiam2 = 36;
standoffChamfer = 1;

// Running clearance between the teeth (mm), the through bores (mm), and the
// small chamfer (mm) that breaks the bores' edges.
backlash = 0.25;
boreDiam1 = 15;
boreDiam2 = 20;
kSmall = 0.25;

// Each gear's faces, measured along its axis from the apex: the back face
// crownToBack past the crown (the outer tooth-tip corner), the toe face recess
// past the toe's tip corner, which lies (1 - faceFraction) of the way out.
outerCone1 = numTeeth1 * moduleVal / (2 * sin(gears.bevelPitchAngle(numTeeth1, numTeeth2, shaftAngle)));
outerCone2 = numTeeth2 * moduleVal / (2 * sin(gears.bevelPitchAngle(numTeeth2, numTeeth1, shaftAngle)));
crown1 = gears.bevelApexToCrown(numTeeth1, numTeeth2, moduleVal, shaftAngle);
crown2 = gears.bevelApexToCrown(numTeeth2, numTeeth1, moduleVal, shaftAngle);
back1 = crown1 + crownToBack;
back2 = crown2 + crownToBack;
toe1 = crown1 * (1 - faceFraction) + recess;
toe2 = crown2 * (1 - faceFraction) + recess;

// Apex at the origin and below the toe face, so the teeth face -Z toward it
// and the hub rises from the back face.
gear1 = shaft.body(
  [shaft.bevel(numTeeth1, numTeeth2, moduleVal, pressureAngle, shaftAngle, spiralAngle,
               outerCone1 * faceFraction, backlash, 0, toe1, back1),
   shaft.chamfer(standoffChamfer),
   shaft.diameter(standoffDiam1, back1, back1 + standoffHeight)],
  drill.chamfer(boreDiam1, kSmall),
  [drill.chamfer(boreDiam1, kSmall), drill.thru(boreDiam1)]);

gear2 = shaft.body(
  [shaft.bevel(numTeeth2, numTeeth1, moduleVal, pressureAngle, shaftAngle, neg(spiralAngle),
               outerCone2 * faceFraction, backlash, 0, toe2, back2),
   shaft.chamfer(standoffChamfer),
   shaft.diameter(standoffDiam2, back2, back2 + standoffHeight)],
  drill.chamfer(boreDiam2, kSmall),
  [drill.chamfer(boreDiam2, kSmall), drill.thru(boreDiam2)]);

// Gear 1 turns about +Z. Gear 2 turns about its own axis, then is swung
// shaftAngle about y so its pitch cone meets gear 1's along the XZ plane, at
// its azimuth pi: gear 1 has a tooth space on its azimuth 0, and a turn of
// pi (n - 1) / n puts a tooth of gear 2 there facing it, for either parity of
// its count.
return transform.rotateZ(gear1, 2 * pi * animate / numTeeth1),
       transform.rotateY(transform.rotateZ(gear2, pi * (numTeeth2 - 1) / numTeeth2 - 2 * pi * animate / numTeeth2), shaftAngle);
